From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:27:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] mb/dell/optiplex_3050: Disable hotplug on the WiFi M.2
 slot too

The WiFi M.2 slot (RP8) is inside the case and can't be hot-swapped
either. With hotplug enabled, Linux's pciehp treats a short link drop
as the card being removed and re-added, so a NIC in this slot
disappears and comes back as a new device, with its bridges. Without
hotplug, the same link drop goes through error recovery and the
device keeps its identity.

bootleg's production machine uses this slot for an Intel I226-V NIC.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb b/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb
index ff48a8121a..911c8c3ba6 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/dell/sklkbl_desktops/variants/optiplex_3050/overridetree.cb
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ chip soc/intel/skylake
 		# M.2 WiFi
 		device ref pcie_rp8 on
 			register "PcieRpClkReqSupport[7]"		= "false"
-			register "PcieRpHotPlug[7]"			= "1"
+			register "PcieRpHotPlug[7]"			= "0"
 		end
 
 		# M.2 SSD
